  "result": "Perfect! All 205 tests pass. I've successfully added payment terms support:\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n\n1. **Added `TERMS_INVALID` error code** to src/errors.js:\n   - \"Payment terms must be 'NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM'.\"\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice()` function** in src/invoices.js:\n   - Accepts optional `terms` parameter ('NET14', 'NET30', or 'EOM')\n   - Defaults to 'NET30' if not provided\n   - Validates terms and calculates dueDate\n   - Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on returned invoice\n   - Returns `TERMS_INVALID` for unknown terms\n\n3. **Added `calculateDueDate()` helper function**:\n   - **NET14**: `dueDate = issueDate + 14 days`\n   - **NET30**: `dueDate = issueDate + 30 days`\n   - **EOM**: `dueDate = last day of issueDate's month`\n   - Handles year boundaries correctly (e.g., Dec 15 \u2192 Dec 31)\n   - Handles leap years (Feb 29 in leap years)\n   - Uses `addDays()` from dates module for UTC calculations\n\n4. **Added 10 comprehensive tests**:\n   - Default NET30 terms\n   - Explicit NET14 terms\n   - Explicit NET30 terms\n   - EOM terms (mid-month, end-of-month, year boundary, December, February with leap year)\n   - Invalid terms rejection\n   - Terms preservation in returned invoice\n\n**Key behaviors:**\n- Terms defaults to 'NET30' when not specified\n- Due dates calculated in UTC using dates module\n- EOM correctly handles month/year boundaries and leap years\n- All invoices now have terms and dueDate properties\n- Invalid terms rejected immediately with TERMS_INVALID error\n\nAll 205 tests pass \u2713",
